    lead: 'A formal letter from a landlord ending a tenancy (for cause or end of lease) or from a tenant giving notice they will leave - stating the last day, move-out requirements and next steps.',
    introParagraphs: ['A notice to vacate tells the other party the tenancy is ending on a specific date. Landlords use it for non-renewal of a lease, end of a month-to-month tenancy or termination for cause; tenants use it to give required notice before moving out.', 'Notice periods are set by state and local law (typically 30, 60 or 90 days; longer in rent-controlled areas). Get the period and delivery method right - a defective notice can restart the clock.'],
    bullets: [['Parties and property', 'Tenant and landlord/manager names, property address and unit.'], ['Reason (if for cause)', 'If terminating for cause (non-payment, lease violation), cite the lease clause and any prior notices; no-cause/end-of-lease notices just state the end date.'], ['Move-out date', 'The date by which the tenant must be out with all belongings and keys returned; calculated from proper service of the notice.'], ['Move-out requirements', 'Cleaning standard, condition expectations, return of keys, forwarding address for the security deposit.'], ['Next steps', 'What happens if the tenant does not leave (eviction filing) or what the landlord will do (inspection, deposit return per local law).']],
    howTo: [['Check required notice period', 'Confirm the minimum notice days and permitted reasons for your jurisdiction and lease type.'], ['Calculate the vacate date', 'Count days from proper service (not mailing); state the exact date.'], ['Cite cause if applicable', 'Reference the lease violation and any prior notices (late rent, unauthorised occupant, etc.).'], ['Deliver as required', 'Hand delivery, posting plus certified mail, or other method required by local law. Email alone is usually insufficient.'], ['Keep proof of service', 'Certificate of service signed by the person delivering, plus postal receipts and photographs.']],
    related: [['Late rent notice', 'templates/late-rent-notice-template.html', 'Pay-or-quit notice when rent is overdue.'], ['Lease termination agreement', 'templates/lease-termination-agreement.html', 'Mutual agreement to end the lease early.'], ['Eviction notice', 'templates/eviction-notice-template.html', 'Court-stage notice after notice to vacate expires.'], ['Security deposit return letter', 'templates/security-deposit-return-letter.html', 'Itemised deductions and refund after move-out.'], ['Free landlord forms', 'for/landlords.html', 'Full landlord/tenant template set.']],
    faq: [['Landlord or tenant can send it?', 'Both - landlords serve it to end a tenancy; tenants send it to give required notice they are leaving.'], ['How much notice?', 'Typically 30-60 days for month-to-month; longer in rent-controlled areas; fixed leases usually expire without notice. Check local law.'], ['Email enough?', 'Rarely. Most jurisdictions require hand delivery, posting and/or certified mail for termination notices.'], ['What if they don\'t leave?', 'You must file eviction (unlawful detainer) in court. Self-help (lockouts, utility shutoffs) is illegal.'], ['Can I revoke the notice?', 'If the tenant agrees in writing - but if they dispute it you may have to start over.']],
