    introParagraphs: ['A lease termination agreement (or mutual move-out agreement) lets a landlord and tenant end a fixed-term lease early by mutual consent instead of eviction or abandonment. It sets the final move-out date, who pays what, and releases both sides from further obligations.', 'Use this when the tenant wants to leave early and the landlord agrees, or when both sides want a clean break. It is cleaner than breaking the lease unilaterally because it waives future rent claims in writing.'],
