    faq: [['Do I have to sign a termination agreement?', 'No — if both sides do not agree, the lease terms and local law govern how either party can end it.'], ['Can the landlord keep the deposit?', 'Only for lawful deductions (unpaid rent, damage beyond normal wear) within the statutory timeframe.'], ['Does it waive back rent?', 'That depends on what you write in the agreement. It can release past unpaid rent or require payment.'], ['Is an early-termination fee legal?', 'Generally yes if it is a reasonable estimate of losses — some states cap fees or require specific language.'], ['What if the tenant does not move out on the agreed date?', 'The agreement is breached — you would typically proceed with eviction per local law.']],
