    lead: 'A written plan between landlord and tenant setting out how overdue rent will be paid back in instalments, while current rent continues to be paid on time.',
    introParagraphs: ['A rent payment plan agreement (or back-rent repayment plan) is used when a tenant has fallen behind and the landlord agrees to accept payment in instalments instead of proceeding straight to eviction. It states how much is owed, instalment amounts, due dates, and what happens if the tenant misses a payment.', 'If local eviction moratoriums or rental-assistance programs apply, follow their documentation requirements. A signed plan protects both sides by putting the agreement in writing.'],
    bullets: [['Parties and property', 'Landlord, tenant, property address and unit.'], ['Arrears amount', 'Total past-due rent and any late fees/charges being rolled into the plan, as of the plan date.'], ['Instalment schedule', 'Amount of each instalment, due dates (often weekly or bi-weekly on top of ongoing rent), total instalments, and final payoff date.'], ['Current rent', 'Statement that normal monthly rent is still due on the regular due date in addition to instalments.'], ['Default terms', 'What happens if an instalment is missed (reinstatement of the original debt, possible eviction filing) and any waiver of late fees.']],
