    introParagraphs: ['A move-in checklist (or move-in/move-out inspection report) records the condition of the rental unit when the tenant moves in. Both landlord and tenant sign it, and it becomes the baseline for deciding what damage to deduct from the security deposit at move-out.', 'Most states require a written move-in inspection, or give the tenant a right to be present at move-out with a similar checklist. Do it every time — even a quick walk-through with photos saves thousands in deposit disputes.'],
